# circleci_orb_namespace (Resource)

Manages a CircleCI orb registry namespace.

A namespace is the globally unique prefix that owns a set of orbs, as in `<namespace>/<orb>`. An organization may own one namespace, and the name is claimed across all of CircleCI rather than only within your organization, so a name another organization already took cannot be created.

A namespace is also what a self-hosted runner resource class is named after: a resource class is always `<namespace>/<class>`. That makes this resource the way to create the namespace a `circleci_runner_resource_class` needs.

!> **Renaming and deleting a namespace are not self-service, in practice.** The v3 API has routes for both (`POST .../rename`, `DELETE ...`), and the provider calls them, but every account this provider's author was able to test — including an organization-admin token on an organization it had just created — received `403 Forbidden` from both, on namespaces both inside and outside the calling account's own organization. CircleCI's support documentation describes a namespace rename or transfer as a support-ticket process, not an API call, and this investigation found no equivalent process documented for deletion at all. Deleting the *organization* that owns a namespace does not delete the namespace either: it is orphaned, keeps existing, and keeps the name claimed with no owner able to act on it again. Treat `name` as permanent once applied, and expect `terraform destroy` on this resource to fail rather than remove anything.

## Availability

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **CircleCI Cloud** | Yes |
| **CircleCI Server** | No — served by the CircleCI v3 API, which a Server installation does not route to its public API service. Using this with `deployment = "server"` reports an explicit error at plan time rather than the confusing HTTP 404 the request would otherwise produce. |
| **API** | `POST /api/v3/namespaces`, `GET /api/v3/namespaces/{id}`, `POST /api/v3/namespaces/{id}/rename` (403 for every account tested; see above), `DELETE /api/v3/namespaces/{id}` (same) |
| **Organization type** | Any. An organization is normally limited to one namespace. |
| **Token** | A personal API token belonging to an organization admin. |

