## Renaming

`name` is **not** a replace-forcing attribute: the v3 API's rename route has the shape of a genuine in-place update (a namespace it succeeds against keeps its id and its orbs), so a `RequiresReplace` here would risk Terraform destroying an organization's only namespace just to satisfy a rename. `name` is left as a plain, non-replacing update instead, specifically so that the outcome measured below is a clean failed apply rather than data loss.

**In practice, expect the rename to fail.** Every attempt this provider's author made against a live account — regardless of which organization owned the namespace or issued the request — answered `403 Forbidden`, and left the namespace's name unchanged. CircleCI's support documentation describes renaming or transferring a namespace as something to request via a support ticket rather than this API call. The error surfaced by Terraform says as much and links to that documentation; a retry with the same configuration will not succeed.

`organization_id` cannot change: a namespace cannot be moved between organizations, so changing it forces a new namespace to be planned. Given the above, do not expect that plan to succeed either, and do not rely on the old namespace being destroyed — see the deletion note at the top of this page.

